field changes.process
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    Anyone can raise a change with Sam. Sam writes down what it costs in scope,
    schedule and budget before anyone decides. Wording and layout inside an agreed
    page are Sam's call. Anything that adds a requirement, moves a milestone, or
    spends contingency over $200 goes to Dana.
field charter.approval
  provenance: specified
  evidence: Signed charter, 2026-09-08
  value: Approved by Dana Reyes, 2026-09-08.
field charter.approval_requirements
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    Dana signs off each milestone. The pilot (M3) is accepted when the front desk
    has run two weeks of real bookings through the system with no double booking
    and Priya confirms her team can use it unaided. Launch (M4) needs Dana's
    written go-ahead.
field charter.budget
  provenance: specified
  evidence: Dana, charter review 2026-09-08
  value: $1,200: $600 plugin licence, $600 contingency. Volunteer time is not charged.
field charter.business_case
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    The binder costs about five staff hours a week and caused two double bookings
    in August. A plugin on the website we already host costs $600 a year, which
    is less than a month of the staff time it replaces. Doing nothing gets worse
    in winter, when room demand roughly doubles.
field charter.decision_rule
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    A decision is recorded with its source: specified (someone with the authority
    said it, and we can quote them), agreed (they approved a written summary), or
    unobjected (proposed, no reply yet). Only specified and agreed count.
field charter.description_deliverables
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    A public booking page on the library website for the community room and the
    study room, a staff calendar view, email templates, a one-page staff guide,
    and the binder's future bookings moved into the new system.
field charter.exit_criteria
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    Close: launched, six weeks of live use, and all four success criteria answered.
    Cancel: County IT refuses the plugin and no approved alternative exists by
    2026-10-02, or the pilot shows the desk spending more time than with the binder.
field charter.high_level_requirements
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    Patrons see which rooms are free and book a slot without an account.
    Staff see every booking in one calendar and can edit or cancel.
    Confirmation and reminder emails to the person who booked.
    Room rules (capacity, hours, no commercial use) shown before booking.
field charter.key_stakeholders
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Charter review, 2026-09-08
  value: |
    Sponsor: Dana Reyes, branch manager.
    PM: Sam Okafor, adult services librarian.
    Front desk team, led by Priya Chen: the heaviest users.
    Leo Martin, IT volunteer: builds and configures.
    County IT web team: approves anything installed on the website.
    Community groups who book regularly, represented by the Friends of the Library.

    Details on the Stakeholder Register screen.
